    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: consolidated duplicate detection into a single `identityKey`\n\n**New identity model** \u2014 `identityKey = normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + householdId`. A create is rejected with **409 only when the new owner's whole identityKey equals an existing owner's**.\n\n### Files added\n- **`OwnerIdentity.java`** \u2014 single source of truth for the key and its parts: `key(telephone, email, householdId)`, `canonicalTelephone` (E.164), `normalizedEmail` (lower-cased, empty when absent), `normalizeName`, and `deriveHouseholdId` (SHA-256 \u2192 `H-\u2026`).\n- **`EnsureIdentityUnique.java`** \u2014 the one duplicate check. It computes the new owner's would-be household component (the derived id when an existing owner shares normalized lastName+address, else empty), builds its identityKey, and compares against every existing owner's key. Household peers are compared using the shared derived id so an exact full-key duplicate is still caught even before back-fill; everyone else uses their stored `householdId`.\n- **`DuplicateIdentityException` / `\u2026Handler`** + escalation YAML \u2192 409 with `{\"errors\":[\"identityKey\"]}`.\n\n### Files changed\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 replaced the three steps (`ensureUniqueTelephone`, `ensureUniqueEmail`, `ensureUniqueHousehold`) with a single `ensureUniqueIdentity`.\n- **`AssignHouseholdId.java`** \u2014 now delegates household-id derivation to `OwnerIdentity` so the assigned id and the check agree exactly.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` property to the `Owner` schema (so it's **returned**).\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 populates `identityKey` from the persisted telephone/email/householdId.\n\n### Files removed\nThe three `Ensure*Unique` functions and the `DuplicateTelephone/Email/Household` exceptions, handlers, and escalation YAMLs.\n\n### Behaviour change (as specified)\nBecause telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with **different telephones now have different identityKeys and are both allowed** \u2014 only an exact full-key match is a duplicate. The former standalone telephone/email/household rejections no longer apply independently.\n\n**Test result:** `BUILD SUCCESS`, `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsIdentityCollision` passes (a second owner reusing the first's telephone with no email and no shared household collides on the whole key \u2192 409).\n\nOne note: the request-only `sharesHousehold` field remains in the OpenAPI schema but is now inert, since the single-key rule replaces the household-opt-in logic. I left the field in place to avoid changing the request contract; let me know if you'd like it removed too.",
